---
id: RL-005
type: rule
family: responsibility-laundering
title: Deferred without artifact
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 4

targets: [agent-output, pr-description, commit-message]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: \b(defer(red)?|follow[\s-]?up|backlog(ged)?)\b(?!.*(issue\s*#|gh\s+issue|TODO|created\s+(issue|ticket)))
  flags: i

related: [RL-002]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Deferral language without a tracking artifact means the work will be
forgotten. "Follow-up" and "backlogged" sound like decisions but are
just labels unless something concrete is created.

Create the artifact: `gh issue create`, add a TODO with a ticket
reference, or create an APS item. If the work genuinely shouldn't be
tracked, ask the user to confirm rather than deciding unilaterally.
